Z||000002||Nashco||10-14-2001||06:23 AM||||I can get past poor punctuation if it's commas and semicolons, but if the period is missing it can make it hard.  A word being spelled wrong usually isn't a big deal, unless the word is unintelligible; when you meant to say things like, "I wasn't painting it because it needed it, I was just bored," for example, but "I want paintin it cause it need it I was juts board," comes out, it can make things confusing.  What does really piss me off, purposeful or not, is when a complete word is missing.  A missing word can make it so you have to read the sentence a few times to figure out what they're trying to say.<P>I just wish people would take an extra minute and re-read their posts before submitting.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
