Z||000026||DKOV||10-15-2001||04:01 AM||||I belong to several forums relating to my varous automotive hobbies.  One thing that I've seen over the past several years is that they ALL, every single one of them, end up in the crapper where "respect" is concerned.<P>It seems like everyone takes offense to the idea of being responsible for their statements and refuses to be "censored".  What ever happened to good taste, respect and responsibility?<P>This is NOT our forum and NOT our money being spent.  Sombody, thank you Pennock, has made it available to us because they share our enthusiasm.  All they have asked in return is for us to follow some simple rules and "play nice".<P>We can THANK them for their hard work by simply respecting their creation.  I think we can all do that... Can't we?<P>Of course, Type-Os are an entirely different thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
